      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOLD BEAU (4) is the one to beat off two sound Belmont Park CL1 efforts, a third over 1700m and then fourth over 1650m when near the top of the betting. His record at this track and around 1920m is the strongest profile in the field, and the easier assignment makes him very appealing. SPACE ACADEMY (3) is the main danger after working home well in a BM58+ at Kalgoorlie and he has already won at this venue. Easier here and from the inside barrier, he'll be hard to hold out. REBELNADO (5) has been plain in two CL3 runs, but both were over shorter trips and he is much better served returning to a distance range where he's won previously. Can bounce back to form. OBSCENTINO (2) was disappointing at Northam last start after winning there the run prior. Expecting a return to form. HANAFUBUKI (1) comes back in trip today and drops right back in grade. Blinkers go back on and an improved effort is on the cards.",
